# Static Solid application

Install the dependencies with the package manager declared in `package.json`.
Bun is required to run the application tasks with every installer.

Run `vp run dev` for development. Run `vp run check:ci`, `vp run test` and
`vp run build` before publishing. After the build, `vp run test:e2e` opens
the generated files in Chromium.

## Publishing

Publish the contents of `.output/public` to a static host with directory
indexes enabled. Each localized URL serves its own HTML. For an unknown path,
serve `404.html` with status 404. Under a locale prefix, serve the corresponding
error page, such as `/pt/404.html`.

The build writes `.output/csp-hashes.json` outside the public directory. Use
the hashes in `pages` for the actual HTML file served, including error pages.
Quote each hash in the `script-src` directive alongside `'self'`. Set
`default-src 'self'`, `style-src 'self'`, `object-src 'none'`,
`base-uri 'self'` and `frame-ancestors 'none'` in the same
`Content-Security-Policy` header. Regenerate the headers on every build.
